  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nMid and high level clouds should erode this morning across the\nregion with enough sunshine for most locations to get into the\n70's for highs. Tonight looks to be the coldest night with high\npressure and clear skies. A few locations falling into the 40's\nis not out of the question. Clouds and moisture will be on the\nincrease though on the backside of the high pressure Saturday.\nEnough lift may be present for some spotty showers by sunset. \n \nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nA warm front will move through the region late Saturday.\nPW values will rise close to 1.5 inches coupled with a decent\nLLJ should provide enough lift for fairly widespread showers.\nCoverage looks highest closer to surface low tracking just to\nour south. The main concern here is that some ensemble members \nand Hires guidance are showing narrow bands of QPF of 1-3 inches\nwith this feature. Localized urban and small stream may become a\npossibility Saturday night for portions of the area if this is\nrealized. With the later timing, instability will be quite \nlimited but an isolated thunderstorm or two cannot be ruled out \nin Northeast PA and the Catskills. \n\nA cold front will soon follow with additional showers and \nstorms. Models are showing around 500 to 1000 J/kg of MLCAPE. If\nthere is a break in showers and some clearing skies early in \nthe day, then these values may be possible. Combined with 30 to \n35 kts of shear, some gusty thunderstorms would then be possible\nSunday afternoon. Mid-level lapse rates are lacking so severe \nstorms are not expected at this time. Showers will linger into \nSunday night and possibly into Monday depending on how quickly \nthe front moves through. High pressure will build in behind the \ndeparture of this system. Temperatures will trend a bit warmer\nthrough the weekend with fairly warm overnight lows Saturday\nnight in the low 60's. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...\n\nOverall, the cold front has trended stronger on model guidance\nwith a more aggressive push of high pressure from Canada early\nnext week. This eliminates the outcome of a very warm Tuesday\nshown the last few days and would bring us more pleasant \ntemperatures from lows in the 50's to highs in the 70's. Also \nthis raises the potential for a more occluded system for the \nmiddle of next week that lacks instability. Some ensemble\nguidance checks up this frontal boundary, so heavy rainfall may\nbecome a concern.",
